===== E318
| Page 165 | 5709 | mssEC 25 (obj 5952, pointer 5709), 28 May 1864 Washington, Eckert to Sheldon: the Gloucester route is best, 100 men can guard that line, Mackintosh's building party, Bickford's operators (FM-R7b; FIX-FM12, AUDIT FV-FM10a s.5; row 5709/1; image-read at 2400 px; whole entry image-read by FV-FM10a)
Geo D Sheldon
Ivory opinion is that the Gloucester route is the best
plunge prolong spit can saddle that line where a whip
could not the other pause unless u know of some
very good reason why it should not be Dunn let
the work be commenced first Peru Mackintosh arrives with his
party & push through fast as Can send Logue &
Embree to Jamestown and hold blissfull & Glazier ready for
white house send Collings to Haven & Homan to Gloucester
if office is needed there zodiac Bickford has some operators
with him who will be stationed at homer send Cowans
with Mackintoshs building party let him come in circuit twice
a day & white progress and inform me all blank
T. T. Eckert
plain-at: white#1
note: FM-R7b: Image-read only down to 'Cowans'; the last lines were transcription only. FIX-FM12 (9 Oct 2026, AUDIT FV-FM10a s.5): the earlier note 'Ivory is probably my; M' is withdrawn: Ivory = General-in-Chief, H (key), identity open (sibling 5709/2; reply 5713/1); '[100] [Men]' may be rendered 'one hundred men'; whole entry image-read by FV-FM10a.
